  "raw": " title\n\nDahlia Jutanugarn overcame a wild drive and a collapse in a bunker to win the Omega Dubai Desert Classic with a second-round 75.\n\nBut she must wait to become the third Thai player in the top 10 - and her country's first-ever winner - after Ariya Jutanugarn lost her title by a stroke.\n\nThitisa Palti led by five strokes on nine under after the first round, but the Indonesian shot a 72 to share second place with American Danielle Kang.\n\nThitisa's best finish this year came at the Women's World Championship before she missed much of 2017 with a back injury.\n\nThitisa fell in the bunker on the 10th and pulled her second shot, but was awarded a two-shot penalty as the ball hit the flag stick.\n\nThe 20-year-old was even par after 13, including an awkward birdie putt from a bunker on Par-3",
  "serialized": "title Dahlia Jutanugarn overcame a wild drive and a collapse in a bunker to win the Omega Dubai Desert Classic with a second-round 75. But she must wait to become the third Thai player in the top 10 - and her country's first-ever winner - after Ariya Jutanugarn lost her title by a stroke. Thitisa Palti led by five strokes on nine under after the first round, but the Indonesian shot a 72 to share second place with American Danielle Kang. Thitisa's best finish this year came at the Women's World Championship before she missed much of 2017 with a back injury. Thitisa fell in the bunker on the 10th and pulled her second shot, but was awarded a two-shot penalty as the ball hit the flag stick. The 20-year-old was even par after 13, including an awkward birdie putt from a bunker on Par-3",
